function choose_risk_treatments(risks, risk_tolerance):
    decisions = empty map

    for each risk in risks:
        risk_score = risk.likelihood * risk.impact

        if risk_score <= risk_tolerance:
            decisions[risk.name] = "accept"
        else if risk.can_stop_activity == true:
            decisions[risk.name] = "avoid"
        else if risk.transfer_available == true and risk.transfer_cost < risk_score:
            decisions[risk.name] = "transfer"
        else if risk.control_available == true and risk.control_cost < risk_score:
            decisions[risk.name] = "mitigate"
        else:
            decisions[risk.name] = "accept with documented exception"

    return decisions
```
A good answer should evaluate likelihood and impact against tolerance, then select avoid, transfer, mitigate, or accept based on feasibility and cost-benefit logic.

